// ============================================================================
// DERIVED RELATION DECLARATIONS — PYTHON rule set.
//
// Base (parser IR) decls live in decls_base.dl and are GENERATED by
// Parser/src/schema/python/gen_decls.py from the frozen fact schema. NEVER hand-write a
// py_* or lib_py_* decl: the column order IS the contract, additions append only, and a
// change needs the human's explicit word.
//
// Everything below is the ENGINE's own. One decl per derived relation, grouped by the
// layer that produces it, in dependency order:
//   projections -> containment -> resolution -> expression-resolution -> call-edge-generation
//
// PROJECTIONS NEVER JOIN. Each projection relation is a named column view over exactly
// one raw base relation, with a leading provenance tag ("client" / "lib"). Interpretation
// is a resolution-layer step, which is why the layers can be tested independently.
//
// Only relations named in export_manifest.tsv are written out; that file is the ONLY
// source of .output. engine/export/*.dl is documentation and is never compiled.
// ============================================================================

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EXECUTOR KNOBS — staged as .input for EVERY language, unconditionally, by
// src/pipeline/run-souffle.sh. They MUST be declared or souffle aborts before a
// single rule runs, with an error that names the .input line rather than the
// missing decl. dispatch_cap is the one that matters here: duck typing widens
// dispatch far more than Java's declared types do.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.decl dispatch_cap(c0:symbol)
.decl jdk_max_depth(c0:number)
.decl lib_max_depth(c0:number)
.decl taint_gating(c0:symbol)


